<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd"><key id="d13" for="edge" attr.name="target_phenomenon" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d12" for="edge" attr.name="source_phenomenon" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="relation_type" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="semantic_rationale" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="scale_direction" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="edge_id" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="units" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="mathematical_definition" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d4" for="node" attr.name="phenomenon_id" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d3" for="node" attr.name="scale" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="schema_version" attr.type="string"/>
<key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="evidence_status" attr.type="string"/>
<graph edgedefault="directed"><data key="d0">unvalidated_semantic_candidates</data>
<data key="d1">2.0</data>
<node id="frag_micro_component_size">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component size of focal fish</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Number of fish in the connected component of the recorded contact graph containing the focal fish at a given step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For run r and step t, let G_t=(V_t,E_t) be the undirected graph with fish nodes V_t from agent_states role='fish' and edges E_t from contacts pairs {agent_id,partner_id} at (r,t). For focal fish i in V_t, let C_t(i) be its connected component in G_t. Indicator = |C_t(i)|.</data>
  <data key="d7">agents</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_micro_isolate">
  <data key="d2">Focal fish contact isolation flag</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Binary flag indicating whether the focal fish has zero recorded contact neighbors at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i at (r,t), let k_i(t)=|{j: (i,j) in E_t or (j,i) in E_t}|. Indicator = 1 if k_i(t)=0, else 0.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_micro_component_shark_distance">
  <data key="d2">Focal component centroid to nearest shark distance</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Distance from the centroid of the focal fish's contact component to the nearest shark at the same step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let c_C(t)=mean_{j in C_t(i)} p_j(t) for focal fish i. Let D_i(t)=min_{s in sharks at t} ||c_C(t)-p_s(t)||. Indicator = D_i(t).</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_meso_mean_component_size">
  <data key="d2">Mean contact-component size</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Average number of fish per connected component of the recorded contact graph at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let components of G_t be C_1,...,C_m. Indicator = (1/m) sum_{k=1}^m |C_k|.</data>
  <data key="d7">agents</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_meso_component_size_entropy">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component size entropy</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Shannon entropy of the distribution of fish counts across connected components at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let p_k=|C_k|/N_t for N_t=sum_j |C_j|. Indicator = -sum_k p_k log2(p_k), with 0 log2 0 treated as 0.</data>
  <data key="d7">bits</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_meso_centroid_pair_distance">
  <data key="d2">Mean distance between component centroids</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Average pairwise Euclidean distance between centroids of distinct contact components at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let c_k be the position centroid of component C_k. Indicator = (2/(m(m-1))) sum_{a&lt;b} ||c_a-c_b|| for m components; undefined if m&lt;2.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_macro_component_count">
  <data key="d2">Number of contact components</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Count of connected components of the recorded fish contact graph at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator = m, the number of connected components of G_t.</data>
  <data key="d7">components</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_macro_largest_fraction">
  <data key="d2">Largest component fish fraction</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of fish belonging to the largest connected component of the contact graph at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator = max_k |C_k| / N_t, where N_t=sum_j |C_j|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="frag_macro_component_count_change">
  <data key="d2">Step change in contact-component count</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">Difference between the number of contact components at the current step and the previous step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator(t)=m(t)-m(t-1), where m(t) is the number of connected components of G_t.</data>
  <data key="d7">components/step</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_micro_major_projection">
  <data key="d2">Focal fish normalized major-axis projection</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Projection of the focal fish position onto the major axis of the whole-school position covariance, scaled by the major-axis standard deviation.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let c=mean_i p_i and C=(1/N) sum_i (p_i-c)(p_i-c)^T for all fish at (r,t). Let lambda1&gt;=lambda2 be eigenvalues and u1 the unit eigenvector for lambda1. For fish i, indicator=(p_i-c)·u1/sqrt(lambda1).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_micro_mahalanobis_sq">
  <data key="d2">Focal fish squared Mahalanobis distance</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Squared Mahalanobis distance of the focal fish position from the whole-school position centroid using the whole-school covariance.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(p_i-c)^T C^{-1}(p_i-c), with c and C as the whole-school position mean and covariance at (r,t).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_micro_component_projection">
  <data key="d2">Focal fish normalized component major-axis projection</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Projection of the focal fish position onto the major axis of its contact component's position covariance, scaled by that component's major-axis standard deviation.</data>
  <data key="d6">For focal fish i in component C_t(i), let c_C, C_C, lambda1_C, u1_C be the component position mean, covariance, largest eigenvalue and eigenvector. Indicator=(p_i-c_C)·u1_C/sqrt(lambda1_C).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_meso_component_aspect_ratio">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component aspect ratio</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Ratio of major to minor axis lengths of the position covariance ellipse for a contact component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k at (r,t), let lambda1&gt;=lambda2 be eigenvalues of its position covariance. Indicator=sqrt(lambda1/lambda2).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_meso_component_escape_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Component major-axis escape alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Absolute cosine between the major axis of a contact component's position covariance and the component mean escape direction from decision records.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, let u1_C be its major-axis unit vector. Let e_C be the normalized mean of decision_json.escape_direction for component fish with non-null escape_direction at (r,t). Indicator=|u1_C·e_C|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_meso_component_axis_length">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component major-axis length</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Standard deviation of fish positions along the major axis of a contact component's position covariance.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=sqrt(lambda1_C), where lambda1_C is the largest eigenvalue of the position covariance of component C_k at (r,t).</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_macro_school_aspect_ratio">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school aspect ratio</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Ratio of major to minor axis lengths of the whole-school position covariance ellipse at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let lambda1&gt;=lambda2 be eigenvalues of the covariance of all fish positions at (r,t). Indicator=sqrt(lambda1/lambda2).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_macro_anisotropy_index">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school anisotropy index</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Normalized difference between major and minor eigenvalues of the whole-school position covariance.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(lambda1-lambda2)/(lambda1+lambda2) for lambda1&gt;=lambda2&gt;0.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="elong_macro_major_escape_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school major-axis escape alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">school_elongation</data>
  <data key="d5">Absolute cosine between the whole-school major axis and the mean escape direction of all fish with recorded escape directions.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let u1 be the whole-school major-axis unit vector. Let e=normalize(sum_i escape_direction_i) over fish with non-null escape_direction at (r,t). Indicator=|u1·e|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_micro_escape_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Focal heading alignment with own escape direction</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Cosine of the angular difference between a fish's recorded heading and its decision-record escape direction at the same step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i with heading theta_i(t) and decision_json.escape_direction e_i(t)=(e_x,e_y), indicator=cos(theta_i(t)-atan2(e_y,e_x)).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_micro_requested_turn_abs">
  <data key="d2">Focal absolute requested turn</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Magnitude of the fish's requested turn angle recorded in the decision JSON.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=|decision_json.requested_turn| for fish i at (r,t).</data>
  <data key="d7">radians</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_micro_heading_change">
  <data key="d2">Focal step heading change magnitude</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Absolute angular change in a fish's heading from the previous step to the current step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=|atan2(sin(theta_i(t)-theta_i(t-1)), cos(theta_i(t)-theta_i(t-1)))|.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_meso_component_escape_coherence">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component escape-direction coherence</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of unit escape-direction vectors within a contact component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, let e_i be unit escape_direction for fish i in C_k with non-null escape_direction. Indicator=|sum_i e_i|/n_k.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_meso_component_mean_escape_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean heading-escape alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean cosine between fish headings and their own escape directions within a contact component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_i cos(theta_i-atan2(e_i_y,e_i_x)) over fish with non-null escape_direction.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_meso_component_turn_variance">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component requested-turn variance</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Variance of requested turn angles across fish in a contact component at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_i (tau_i - mean_j tau_j)^2, where tau_i=decision_json.requested_turn.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians^2</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_macro_school_escape_coherence">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school escape-direction coherence</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of all fish unit escape-direction vectors at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=|sum_i e_i|/n, over fish with non-null escape_direction at (r,t).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_macro_heading_change_shark_cov">
  <data key="d2">Heading-change magnitude vs shark proximity covariance</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Empirical covariance across fish between step heading-change magnitude and inverse distance to the nearest shark.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i at (r,t) with d_i&gt;0, let x_i=|Delta theta_i| and y_i=1/d_i. Indicator=(1/n) sum_i (x_i-mean x)(y_i-mean y).</data>
  <data key="d7">radians per model length</data>
</node>
<node id="wave_macro_escape_coherence_change">
  <data key="d2">Step change in school escape-direction coherence</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Difference between whole-school escape-direction coherence at the current step and the previous step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator(t)=R(t)-R(t-1), where R(t)=|sum_i e_i(t)|/n(t) over non-null escape directions.</data>
  <data key="d7">1/step</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_micro_state">
  <data key="d2">Focal fish frightened indicator</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Binary indicator that the focal fish has a nonzero fright episode value at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=1 if fright_i(t)&gt;0, else 0.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_micro_remaining">
  <data key="d2">Focal remaining fright steps</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Number of fright steps remaining after the current update for the focal fish.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=remaining_i(t) for fish i.</data>
  <data key="d7">steps</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_micro_nearest_fright_distance">
  <data key="d2">Focal distance to nearest frightened contact neighbor</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Minimum Euclidean distance from a fish to any of its recorded contact neighbors that are frightened at the same step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i, let N_i(t) be contact neighbors at (r,t) with fright_j(t)&gt;0. Indicator=min_{j in N_i(t)} ||p_i(t)-p_j(t)||.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_meso_component_prevalence">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component fright prevalence</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of fish in a contact component that are frightened at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/|C_k|) sum_{i in C_k} 1[fright_i(t)&gt;0].</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_meso_component_fright_edge_fraction">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component frightened-edge fraction</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of within-component contact edges whose two endpoints are both frightened.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, let E_k(t) be recorded edges with both endpoints in C_k. Indicator=|{(i,j) in E_k: fright_i&gt;0 and fright_j&gt;0}|/|E_k|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_meso_component_fright_position_corr">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component fright-centroid-distance correlation</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Pearson correlation across component fish between fright indicator and distance to the component centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, let x_i=1[fright_i&gt;0] and y_i=||p_i-c_C||. Indicator=corr(x,y) over i in C_k.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_macro_school_prevalence">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school fright prevalence</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of all fish that are frightened at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t) sum_i 1[fright_i(t)&gt;0] over all fish i.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_macro_school_fright_edge_fraction">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school frightened-edge fraction</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of all recorded contact edges whose two endpoints are both frightened.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=|{(i,j) in E_t: fright_i&gt;0 and fright_j&gt;0}|/|E_t|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="fright_macro_onset_rate">
  <data key="d2">Fright onset rate</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">fright_contagion_wave</data>
  <data key="d5">Number of fish transitioning from not frightened to frightened per step divided by the number of fish with both states defined.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=|{i: fright_i(t)&gt;0 and fright_i(t-1)=0}|/N_t^defined.</data>
  <data key="d7">1/step</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_micro_heading_deviation">
  <data key="d2">Focal heading deviation from school mean</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Absolute angular difference between a fish's heading and the whole-school mean heading at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let Theta=atan2(mean_i sin theta_i, mean_i cos theta_i). Indicator=|atan2(sin(theta_i-Theta), cos(theta_i-Theta))|.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_micro_neighbor_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Focal heading alignment with contact neighbors</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Cosine between a fish's heading and the mean heading of its recorded contact neighbors.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i, let N_i(t) be contact neighbors. Let theta_N=atan2(mean_{j in N_i} sin theta_j, mean_{j in N_i} cos theta_j). Indicator=cos(theta_i-theta_N).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_micro_shark_proximity">
  <data key="d2">Focal inverse distance to nearest shark</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Reciprocal of the distance from a fish to the nearest shark at the same step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=1/d_i(t), where d_i(t)=min_{s in sharks} ||p_i(t)-p_s(t)||&gt;0.</data>
  <data key="d7">1/model length</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_meso_component_polarization">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component heading polarization</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of fish heading unit vectors within a contact component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=sqrt((sum_i cos theta_i)^2+(sum_i sin theta_i)^2)/|C_k|.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_meso_component_mean_deviation">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean heading deviation</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean absolute angular deviation of component fish headings from the component mean heading.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let Theta_C=atan2(mean_{i in C} sin theta_i, mean_{i in C} cos theta_i). Indicator=(1/|C|) sum_{i in C} |atan2(sin(theta_i-Theta_C), cos(theta_i-Theta_C))|.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_meso_component_away_shark_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component heading away-from-shark alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Cosine between the component mean heading vector and the unit vector from the nearest shark to the component centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let Theta_C be component mean heading and c_C its centroid. Let s* be the nearest shark to c_C and a=(c_C-p_s*)/||c_C-p_s*||. Indicator=cos(Theta_C)·a_x+sin(Theta_C)·a_y.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_macro_school_polarization">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school heading polarization</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of all fish heading unit vectors at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=sqrt((sum_i cos theta_i)^2+(sum_i sin theta_i)^2)/N_t.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_macro_polarization_proximity_cov">
  <data key="d2">Run-level polarization vs mean shark proximity covariance</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Run-level empirical covariance across sampled steps between whole-school heading polarization and mean inverse nearest-shark distance.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let R(t) be school polarization and q(t)=(1/N_t) sum_i 1/d_i(t). Indicator=(1/T) sum_t (R(t)-mean R)(q(t)-mean q) over steps with both defined.</data>
  <data key="d7">1/model length</data>
</node>
<node id="pol_macro_polarization_change">
  <data key="d2">Step change in whole-school polarization</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">threat_induced_polarization</data>
  <data key="d5">Difference between whole-school heading polarization at the current step and the previous step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator(t)=R(t)-R(t-1), where R(t) is the whole-school heading polarization.</data>
  <data key="d7">1/step</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_micro_degree">
  <data key="d2">Focal contact degree</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Number of distinct recorded contact neighbors of a fish at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i, indicator=k_i(t)=|{j: (i,j) in E_t or (j,i) in E_t}|.</data>
  <data key="d7">neighbors</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_micro_nearest_contact_distance">
  <data key="d2">Focal nearest contact-neighbor distance</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Minimum Euclidean distance from a fish to any of its recorded contact neighbors.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i, indicator=min_{j in N_i(t)} ||p_i(t)-p_j(t)||.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_micro_clustering_coefficient">
  <data key="d2">Focal local clustering coefficient</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Local clustering coefficient of a fish in the undirected recorded contact graph.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let k_i be degree and T_i the number of edges among neighbors of i in G_t. Indicator=2T_i/(k_i(k_i-1)) if k_i&gt;=2.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_meso_component_edge_density">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component edge density</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Recorded contact edges within a component divided by the number of possible unordered fish pairs in that component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k with n_k=|C_k| and e_k=|E_k|, indicator=e_k/(n_k(n_k-1)/2).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_meso_component_mean_degree">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean degree</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean contact degree of fish belonging to a contact component, using the full recorded contact graph at the step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} k_i(t).</data>
  <data key="d7">neighbors</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_meso_component_mean_nearest_distance">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean nearest-contact distance</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean over component fish of the distance to each fish's nearest recorded contact neighbor.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} min_{j in N_i(t)} ||p_i-p_j|| over fish with N_i(t) nonempty.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_macro_school_mean_degree">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school mean contact degree</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean recorded contact degree across all fish at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t) sum_i k_i(t).</data>
  <data key="d7">neighbors</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_macro_school_clustering">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school global clustering coefficient</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Global clustering coefficient of the undirected recorded contact graph at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=3T_t/Q_t, where T_t is the number of triangles and Q_t the number of connected triples in G_t.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="comp_macro_school_mean_nearest_distance">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school mean nearest-contact distance</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">local_compaction</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean over all fish of the distance to each fish's nearest recorded contact neighbor.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t^c) sum_i min_{j in N_i(t)} ||p_i-p_j|| over fish with N_i(t) nonempty.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_micro_angular_velocity">
  <data key="d2">Focal angular velocity around school centroid</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Signed angular velocity of a fish around the whole-school centroid implied by its position and velocity.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let r_i=p_i-c_school and v_i=(vx_i,vy_i). Indicator=(r_i_x v_i_y - r_i_y v_i_x)/||r_i||^2.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_micro_tangential_speed">
  <data key="d2">Focal signed tangential speed</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Signed tangential component of fish velocity around the whole-school centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(r_i_x v_i_y - r_i_y v_i_x)/||r_i||.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_micro_radial_velocity">
  <data key="d2">Focal radial velocity</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Radial component of fish velocity relative to the whole-school centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(r_i_x v_i_x + r_i_y v_i_y)/||r_i||.</data>
  <data key="d7">model length/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_meso_component_angular_velocity">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean angular velocity</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean signed angular velocity of component fish around the component centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k with centroid c_C, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} ((p_i-c_C)_x v_i_y-(p_i-c_C)_y v_i_x)/||p_i-c_C||^2.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_meso_component_rotational_order">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component rotational order</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of unit tangential direction vectors of component fish around the component centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let t_i=(-(p_i-c_C)_y,(p_i-c_C)_x)/||p_i-c_C||. Indicator=||(1/n_k) sum_i t_i||.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_meso_component_angular_momentum">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean angular momentum</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean cross product of component-relative position and velocity across component fish.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} ((p_i-c_C)_x v_i_y-(p_i-c_C)_y v_i_x).</data>
  <data key="d7">model length^2/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_macro_school_angular_velocity">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school mean angular velocity</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean signed angular velocity of all fish around the whole-school centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t) sum_i ((p_i-c)_x v_i_y-(p_i-c)_y v_i_x)/||p_i-c||^2.</data>
  <data key="d7">radians/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_macro_school_rotational_order">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school rotational order</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Resultant length of unit tangential direction vectors of all fish around the whole-school centroid.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let t_i=(-(p_i-c)_y,(p_i-c)_x)/||p_i-c||. Indicator=||(1/N_t) sum_i t_i||.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="mill_macro_school_angular_momentum">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school mean angular momentum</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">vortex_milling</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean cross product of school-relative position and velocity across all fish.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t) sum_i ((p_i-c)_x v_i_y-(p_i-c)_y v_i_x).</data>
  <data key="d7">model length^2/model time</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_micro_lagged_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Focal lagged neighbor heading-change alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Cosine between a fish's current heading change and the mean heading change of its previous-step contact neighbors.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let Delta theta_i(t)=atan2(sin(theta_i(t)-theta_i(t-1)), cos(theta_i(t)-theta_i(t-1))). For N_i(t-1), let m_i(t-1)=mean_{j in N_i(t-1)} Delta theta_j(t-1). Indicator=cos(Delta theta_i(t)-m_i(t-1)).</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_micro_influence_score">
  <data key="d2">Focal run-level lagged influence score</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Run-level Pearson correlation for a focal fish between its heading change at a step and the mean heading change of its contact neighbors at the next step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For fish i, let x_t=Delta theta_i(t) and y_t=mean_{j in N_i(t)} Delta theta_j(t+1). Indicator=corr(x_t,y_t) over valid t in the run.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_micro_influence_percentile">
  <data key="d2">Focal run-level influence percentile</data>
  <data key="d3">micro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Percentile rank of a focal fish's run-level lagged influence score among all fish in the same run.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=100*(rank(s_i)-0.5)/M, where s_i is the influence score and M is the number of fish with defined scores in the run.</data>
  <data key="d7">percentile</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_meso_component_lagged_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component mean lagged heading-change alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean over component fish of the lagged neighbor heading-change alignment at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} cos(Delta theta_i(t)-m_i(t-1)), with m_i(t-1) the mean previous-step neighbor heading change.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_meso_component_cascade_fraction">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component sign-matched cascade fraction</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of component fish whose current heading-change sign matches the sign of the component mean heading change at the previous step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let M_C(t-1)=mean_{j in C_k(t-1)} Delta theta_j(t-1). Indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k(t)} 1[sign(Delta theta_i(t))=sign(M_C(t-1))].</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_meso_component_influence_variance">
  <data key="d2">Contact-component influence-score variance</data>
  <data key="d3">meso</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Run-level variance of fish lagged influence scores within a contact component.</data>
  <data key="d6">For component C_k, indicator=(1/n_k) sum_{i in C_k} (s_i-mean_{j in C_k} s_j)^2, where s_i is the run-level lagged influence score.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless^2</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_macro_school_lagged_alignment">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school mean lagged heading-change alignment</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Mean over all fish of the lagged neighbor heading-change alignment at a step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/N_t^d) sum_i cos(Delta theta_i(t)-m_i(t-1)) over fish with defined lagged alignment.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_macro_school_cascade_fraction">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school sign-matched cascade fraction</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Fraction of fish whose current heading-change sign matches the sign of the whole-school mean heading change at the previous step.</data>
  <data key="d6">Let M(t-1)=mean_j Delta theta_j(t-1). Indicator=(1/N_t) sum_i 1[sign(Delta theta_i(t))=sign(M(t-1))].</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless</data>
</node>
<node id="lead_macro_school_influence_variance">
  <data key="d2">Whole-school influence-score variance</data>
  <data key="d3">macro</data>
  <data key="d4">leader_follower_cascade</data>
  <data key="d5">Run-level variance of fish lagged influence scores across all fish in a run.</data>
  <data key="d6">Indicator=(1/M) sum_i (s_i-mean_j s_j)^2 over fish i with defined run-level influence score s_i.</data>
  <data key="d7">dimensionless^2</data>
</node>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="frag_meso_component_size_entropy">
  <data key="d8">upward__b00_r0000</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Fish in larger contact components exert stronger social attraction, promoting further aggregation and reducing the number of small components, which lowers component-size entropy.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="wave_meso_component_mean_escape_alignment">
  <data key="d8">upward__b00_r0001</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">In larger components, social alignment with many neighbors can dilute individual escape responses, reducing the component's mean escape alignment.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="pol_meso_component_mean_deviation">
  <data key="d8">upward__b00_r0002</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Larger components encompass more diverse headings due to weaker local coordination, increasing the mean heading deviation within the component.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">threat_induced_polarization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="mill_meso_component_rotational_order">
  <data key="d8">upward__b00_r0003</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Larger components provide more individuals to sustain collective rotation, enhancing rotational order.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">vortex_milling</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="comp_micro_degree">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b00_r0000</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">A fish embedded in a larger connected component has more potential contact partners, so its realized contact degree tends to be higher.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">local_compaction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="comp_micro_nearest_contact_distance">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b00_r0001</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">Larger connected components usually arise from denser local spacing, which reduces the distance to the nearest contact neighbor.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">local_compaction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="pol_micro_neighbor_alignment">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b00_r0002</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">More neighbors in a larger component increase the social alignment pressure on a fish, raising alignment with nearby headings.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">threat_induced_polarization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="fright_micro_nearest_fright_distance">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b00_r0003</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">Belonging to a larger component increases the chance that a frightened neighbor is nearby, reducing the distance to the nearest frightened contact.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">fright_contagion_wave</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_size" target="lead_micro_influence_score">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b00_r0004</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">Fish in larger components have more opportunities to affect neighbors' future turns, which can raise their run-level lagged influence score.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">leader_follower_cascade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_isolate" target="frag_meso_centroid_pair_distance">
  <data key="d8">upward__b01_r0000</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Isolated fish can act as outlying singleton components when local avoidance or escape separates them from neighbors; their centroids then sit farther from the main component centroids, raising the mean distance between component centroids at the meso scale.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="frag_meso_component_size_entropy">
  <data key="d8">upward__b02_r0000</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Components whose centroids are near a shark experience stronger escape pressure; this can cause uneven local splitting or merging across the school, changing how fish counts are distributed among components and thus component-size entropy.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="frag_meso_centroid_pair_distance">
  <data key="d8">upward__b02_r0001</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">When some components are much closer to the shark than others, differential escape responses can push their centroids apart or pull them together, altering the mean separation between component centroids.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="pol_meso_component_polarization">
  <data key="d8">upward__b02_r0002</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">A component near a shark may align headings more strongly as fish flee, while farther components retain social headings; component-level polarization can therefore depend on how close the focal component is to the shark.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">threat_induced_polarization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="frag_macro_component_count">
  <data key="d8">upward__b02_r0003</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">Many local component-shark encounters can induce localized breakaways and regrouping, which aggregate into changes in the number of connected components across the whole school.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="frag_macro_largest_fraction">
  <data key="d8">upward__b02_r0004</data>
  <data key="d9">upward</data>
  <data key="d10">If components near sharks split off or are stretched away from the main body, the share of fish in the largest component can shrink; thus local threat distance can shape macro fragmentation.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="frag_micro_isolate">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b02_r0000</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">A component centroid closer to a shark can intensify local avoidance and detachment of fringe fish, making focal contact isolation more likely.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">school_fragmentation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="comp_micro_nearest_contact_distance">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b02_r0001</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">Threat proximity to a component centroid can compress or loosen local spacing as fish adjust repulsion and attraction, altering nearest-contact distance.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">local_compaction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="frag_micro_component_shark_distance" target="wave_micro_heading_change">
  <data key="d8">intra_scale__b02_r0002</data>
  <data key="d9">intra_scale</data>
  <data key="d10">A closer shark near the component centroid can evoke stronger focal turning responses, increasing step heading change.</data>
  <data key="d11">semantic_candidate</data>
  <data key="d12">school_fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d13">coordinated_escape_wave</data>
